You have a fourth nerve palsy in one eye. This means the fourth cranial nerve, which controls the superior oblique muscle, is not working normally.\
\
When that muscle is weakened, the eyes may not stay aligned properly, especially in down-gaze or when reading, going downstairs, or tilting the head. This often causes vertical double vision, and many people instinctively tilt their head to reduce the doubling.\
\
A fourth nerve palsy may be congenital and only become more noticeable later in life, or it may be acquired from causes such as head trauma, reduced blood flow to the nerve, or other neurological conditions. Further assessment is sometimes needed to determine the cause.\
\
